    <div class="privacy-body">

        <section id="overview" class="policy-section">
            <h2>1. Overview</h2>
            <div class="policy-highlight">
                <p><strong>Receipt Vault is built privacy-first.</strong> Your receipts — the photos and the details — are stored <strong>on your device</strong>, and text recognition happens <strong>on your device</strong>. We don't collect your name, email or payment details. The only thing our server stores is a record that a purchase is valid.</p>
            </div>
            <p>This policy explains what information Receipt Vault handles, how, and your rights over it. It applies to the Receipt Vault iOS app and this website. By using Receipt Vault you confirm you have read and understood it.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="who-we-are" class="policy-section">
            <h2>2. Who We Are</h2>
            <p>Receipt Vault is published by <strong>Far Above Studios</strong> ("we", "us", "our"). For data entered into the app and kept on your device, you are the controller — the data never leaves your device. For the limited data our server processes (anonymous purchase records only), we are the data controller under UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018. Cloud backup, if you enable it, uses your own iCloud account and is handled by Apple — not us.</p>
            <div class="policy-info-box">
                <p><strong>Email:</strong> farabovestudios&#64;gmail.com</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="data" class="policy-section">
            <h2>3. Information We Handle</h2>
            <h3>3.1 Receipt content (on your device)</h3>
            <p>Photos you capture and the details recognised or entered — merchant, total, date, category, line items, notes and tags — are stored locally on your device. Deleting the app removes this local data.</p>
            <h3>3.2 Purchase information</h3>
            <p>When you buy the one-time Premium unlock, Apple processes the payment. To confirm the purchase is genuine and keep your features unlocked, the app sends the purchase's <strong>transaction identifier</strong> to our server, which validates it with Apple and stores the entitlement (the transaction identifier, the product purchased, and whether it is active). This record contains <strong>no name, email, payment details or receipt content</strong>, and is not used to track you.</p>
            <h3>3.3 Diagnostics</h3>
            <p>The app includes no third-party analytics or advertising SDKs. Apple may share aggregate, anonymous crash and usage statistics with us if you have opted in to sharing these with developers in your device settings.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="on-device" class="policy-section">
            <h2>4. On-Device Processing</h2>
            <p>Reading the merchant, total and line items from a receipt is performed <strong>on your device</strong> using Apple's on-device frameworks. Your receipt images are not uploaded to be processed.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="use" class="policy-section">
            <h2>5. How We Use Information</h2>
            <p>We use information only to provide and operate the app; recognise and organise your receipts; validate purchases and unlock the features you've paid for; and, if you enable it, back up and sync your receipts through your own iCloud. We do not sell your information or use it for advertising.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="cloud" class="policy-section">
            <h2>6. iCloud Backup &amp; Sync (Premium)</h2>
            <p>If you buy Premium and turn on backup, your receipts are backed up and kept in sync across your devices through <strong>your own iCloud account</strong>. This uses Apple's iCloud — <strong>we do not store your receipts on our servers and never hold a copy</strong>. You control this data in your iCloud settings and can delete it at any time (see <a href="/privacy#retention">Retention &amp; Deletion</a>).</p>
        </section>

        <section id="third-parties" class="policy-section">
            <h2>7. Third Parties</h2>
            <p><strong>Apple</strong> processes payments, provides the App Store, and provides the iCloud where your backup lives if you enable it — under Apple's own privacy policy. <strong>Microsoft Azure</strong> hosts our purchase-validation server, which stores only anonymous purchase records (never your receipts), in Azure's <strong>UK West</strong> region, with Microsoft acting as our processor. We use no advertising networks or data brokers.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="payments" class="policy-section">
            <h2>8. Payments</h2>
            <p>All payments are handled by Apple through the App Store. We never receive or store your card or payment details.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="retention" class="policy-section">
            <h2>9. Retention &amp; Deletion</h2>
            <p><strong>On-device data</strong> stays until you delete individual receipts or the app. <strong>Purchase records</strong> are kept while the entitlement is active and for a reasonable period after, to support restores, refunds and our legal obligations. <strong>iCloud backup data</strong> lives in your own iCloud — you can delete it at any time from within the app or from your iCloud settings, and it is governed by Apple's retention as well.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="security" class="policy-section">
            <h2>10. Security</h2>
            <p>Data in transit is protected with HTTPS/TLS, and cloud-stored data is encrypted at rest. No system is perfectly secure, but we take reasonable measures to protect your information.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="rights" class="policy-section">
            <h2>11. Your Rights</h2>
            <p>If you are in the UK or EU, you have rights under the UK GDPR / GDPR — to access, correct, delete, or restrict processing of your personal data, and to object to processing. Because most data is on your device, you can exercise many of these directly in the app. For cloud data or purchase records, email us. You may also complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office (ICO).</p>
        </section>

        <section id="transfers" class="policy-section">
            <h2>12. International Transfers</h2>
            <p>Our purchase-validation server is located in the UK (Azure UK West). iCloud backup is stored by Apple under Apple's own infrastructure and terms. If you use the app from outside the UK, the limited purchase data may be processed in the UK under appropriate safeguards.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="children" class="policy-section">
            <h2>13. Children</h2>
            <p>Receipt Vault is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect data from them.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="changes" class="policy-section">
            <h2>14. Changes</h2>
            <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by the "Last updated" date above and, where appropriate, noted in the app.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="contact" class="policy-section">
            <h2>15. Contact</h2>
            <p>Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:farabovestudios@gmail.com">farabovestudios&#64;gmail.com</a>.</p>
        </section>

